# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
venv/
.venv/

# Mac
.DS_Store

# Third-party material captured for verification. NOT redistributed.
# sources/ holds the full text of another author's master's thesis
# (131 pp, licensed CC BY-NC-ND) and saved captures of a commercial
# vendor's website. Redistributing them adds nothing to reproducibility,
# so this repository publishes the provenance record instead:
# provenance/sources-provenance.md gives the retrieval URL, date, method
# and integrity hash for every file, and provenance/CHECKSUMS.txt lets a
# reader confirm that a re-retrieved copy is byte-identical to ours.
sources/

# Retrieved article full text, one file per work. Same decision as sources/:
# these are third-party articles, and republishing an author's text is not what
# makes this study reproducible. data/fulltext_log.csv publishes the part that
# does — which URL served each work, on what date, how much text it yielded,
# and why a retrieval failed — so a reader can re-retrieve the same documents.
fulltext/

# Per-coder raw output, one JSON per work per coder. Intermediate: everything a
# reader needs to recompute kappa or check a code against the text is published
# in data/classification.csv, which carries both coders' codes and the located
# quotes. These files additionally hold longer stretches of third-party text.
coding_raw/

# Internal development documents (series convention: not published)
PLAN.md
PLAN-DEVIATIONS.md
LITERATURE.md
RESEARCH-*.md
REVIEW-REPORT*.md
GPT-REVIEW-*.md

# The shared Vancouver-style reference checker writes here. Its DOI resolution is
# sound but its field verdicts are computed on a template this manuscript's
# author-date references do not follow, so its report reads as a list of
# mismatches that are parser artifacts. Publishing it would mislead. The
# applicable check is output/reference_verification_by_doi.md, from
# src/verify_manuscript_refs.py, which is published.
output/reference_verification.md
output/reference_verification.json
